1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,550
Every non-trivial zero of the Riemann zeta function has real part one half.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,525
That is the Riemann Hypothesis.

3
00:00:06,525 --> 00:00:18,675
In November 2026, a Lean 4 formalization of the statement, and of its generalization to Dirichlet L-functions, was released: one hundred seventy-five thousand modules, seventeen million lines.

4
00:00:18,675 --> 00:00:21,987
This is a replay and consolidation of that archive.

5
00:00:21,987 --> 00:00:23,525
It is not a new proof.

6
00:00:23,525 --> 00:00:30,900
The working tree we build has forty-seven thousand eight hundred eighty-five modules and fourteen point five eight million lines.

7
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:36,025
We parse every import: four hundred ninety-four thousand nine hundred forty-seven edges.

8
00:00:36,025 --> 00:00:38,125
The graph is not an illustration.

9
00:00:38,125 --> 00:00:39,512
It is the source tree.

10
00:00:39,512 --> 00:00:45,037
We build two targets, Main and Challenge, in a Linux container on an Apple M4 Max.

11
00:00:45,037 --> 00:01:05,537
The successful run: one hundred fourteen thousand and nineteen jobs, nine hours seven minutes, zero errors, exit zero, at commit e four nine seven a six six zero three e. Lake still generates intermediate representation: four hundred sixty-four gigabytes of dot I R and dot C files, against seventy-three gigabytes of oleans.

12
00:01:05,537 --> 00:01:12,475
The elabArts target does not suppress I R, because importers request meta export info, which pulls I R arts.

13
00:01:12,475 --> 00:01:14,537
Disk headroom is part of the build.

14
00:01:14,537 --> 00:01:16,487
The graph is wide and shallow.

15
00:01:16,487 --> 00:01:21,712
Mean degree twenty point seven; median ten; maximum four thousand two hundred nine.

16
00:01:21,712 --> 00:01:25,662
The deepest k-core is forty-six, with only twenty-one modules.

17
00:01:25,662 --> 00:01:29,287
The longest import chain is one hundred fifty-six modules.

18
00:01:29,287 --> 00:01:38,650
But the critical path is not the bottleneck: its measured cost is about twenty-four minutes, against six point two five hours of total work on sixteen cores.

19
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:40,362
Compile cost is broad.

20
00:01:40,362 --> 00:01:45,662
Total measured median time: four hundred seventeen thousand three hundred forty-one seconds.

21
00:01:45,662 --> 00:01:49,362
The top one percent of modules account for nine point seven percent.

22
00:01:49,362 --> 00:01:53,050
Modules of degree three to fifty account for eighty-five percent.

23
00:01:53,050 --> 00:01:56,637
The build is throughput-bound, not dominated by a few hubs.

24
00:01:56,637 --> 00:02:05,375
Ollivier Ricci curvature on all four hundred ninety-four thousand edges: mean minus zero point two six six; ninety point nine percent negative.

25
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:12,300
Cross namespace edges are more negative: minus zero point three five, against minus zero point two five.

26
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:20,350
The sharpest bridges sit between Development dot Abelian Variety Theory and its neighbours, and between Formalism and Reciprocity Theory.

27
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:23,787
These are interface boundaries, not compile time hotspots.

28
00:02:23,787 --> 00:02:33,862
Instance debt: eighteen thousand eight hundred fifteen attribute minus instance lines across ten thousand three hundred forty-four modules, twenty-one point six percent of the tree.

29
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:42,425
Strict near duplicate census: four hundred forty-four modules at cosine at least zero point nine five and Jaccard at least zero point eight.

30
00:02:42,425 --> 00:02:44,512
Both are generator level problems.

31
00:02:44,512 --> 00:02:45,900
The build is green.

32
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:48,162
That is not the same as certification.

33
00:02:48,162 --> 00:02:56,462
Certification requires a clean worktree, a clean build, exports, the comparator, con leche, and the paranoid checker.

34
00:02:56,462 --> 00:02:59,512
At the time of this recording, the export is still running.

35
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:00,550
Build green.

36
00:03:00,550 --> 00:03:02,550
Certification in progress.

37
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:03,937
The graph is real.

38
00:03:03,937 --> 00:03:05,750
The proof is the next step.

